+# DOT senior staff and congressional recipient records for the FAA follow-up trail
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · B129 / PD01–PD04
+
+Kenneth Mead's prepared statement to a House subcommittee describes DOT follow-up on recommendations and identifies **senior staff meetings attended by heads of DOT operating administrations** as a place where the Secretary reinforced attention to inspector-general findings. This statement is in the printed hearing's scanned pages, beyond the available HTML transcript. Mead says he resigned in **February 2006**. The FAA referral report is dated **August 31, 2006** and names **Todd J. Zinser**, Acting Inspector General, as sender. The testimony supplies a record series to check across the transition. It gives no case-specific agenda, assignment, direction or disposition. [House hearing, physical pp. 69–71](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=69) · [FAA referral memorandum, p. 1](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=1)
+
+## The two routing leads
+
+- **DOT Secretary and operating administrations.** In the prepared statement, Mead discusses both audit and investigative findings before describing follow-up to see whether recommendations were implemented and reporting to the Secretary and Congress when they were not. He separately describes the senior staff meetings. The oral remarks emphasize the dual reporting relationship, regular access to the Secretary and congressional oversight. None of these passages identifies the follow-up procedure for the August referral. Seek senior staff agenda packets, attendance and action-item logs, written Secretary or FAA assignments, and OIG updates keyed to the case. [Prepared statement, physical pp. 70–71, printed pp. 66–67](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=70) · [Oral remarks, physical pp. 66–67](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=66)
+- **Legislative receipt and review.** Eleanor Hill recalls earlier Senate Governmental Affairs Committee staff review of each IG semiannual report. The House's **3550** referral names the **House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform** and concerns a **Secretary's management report** for the period ending **March 31, 2007**. Those are distinct recipients and document categories. NARA's historical guide describes direct committee referrals in §24.14 and identifies executive communications, calendars, minutes and distinct subject files among predecessor committee papers in §§11.99–11.101. The described **47 feet** of executive communications is in the predecessor grouping for **1953–1968**. The guides leave 110th Congress custody open. A receiving-committee executive communication register and DOT outgoing control sheet would test the 3550 delivery and exact enclosure. [Hill discussion, physical p. 116](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=116) · [House 3550, physical p. 104](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GPO-HJOURNAL-2007/pdf/GPO-HJOURNAL-2007-2-2.pdf#page=104) · [House Clerk guide, §24.14](https://www.archives.gov/legislative/guide/house/chapter-24.html) · [Committee guide, §§11.99–11.101](https://www.archives.gov/legislative/guide/house/chapter-11.html)
+
+## Source distinctions retained
+
+| Field | Observations with their scope |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Hearing title** | The printed hearing cover gives **Inspectors General: Independence and Integrity**. Hill's prepared statement face and the House committee's activities report call the June 20 hearing **Inspectors General: Independence and Accountability**. Both title strings are search keys. [Hearing cover](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=1) · [Hill face, physical p. 56](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=56) · [Activities report, printed p. 99, physical p. 107](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CRPT-110hrpt930/pdf/CRPT-110hrpt930.pdf#page=107) |
+| **Time labels** | Mead's statement prints **Expected at 2:00p.m. EST**. The transcript opening records the subcommittee meeting at **2:05 p.m.** without a time-zone label in that line. Expected release time and reported meeting start are different fields. [Mead face](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=69) · [Transcript opening](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=5) |
+| **Institutional roles** | The 2007 hearing introduction calls Hill **Staff Director of the 9/11 Commission**. The 2002 congressional hearing identifies her as **Staff Director, Joint Inquiry Staff**. The Commission's own site identifies Philip Zelikow as its **Executive Director**. Preserve the attributions and keep the Joint Inquiry and Commission record series distinct. [2007 introduction, physical p. 51](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=51) · [Joint Inquiry hearing, printed p. 58 and following statement](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-107jhrg96166/pdf/CHRG-107jhrg96166.pdf) · [Commission biography](https://www.9-11commission.gov/about/bio_zelikow.htm) |
+| **DOT OIG personnel records** | Mead's written statement uses **Cal Scoville** for his successor. The first semiannual report uses **Calvin L. Scovel III** and gives **October 27, 2006** for swearing-in. The August referral memorandum identifies **Todd J. Zinser** as Acting Inspector General. Keep the names, roles and dates with their own records. The handoff of the specific investigation remains unacquired. [Mead face](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=69) · [First semiannual report, physical p. 5](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/trans4_SAR1H_09_072307_508_compliant.pdf#page=5) · [August referral cover](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=1) |
+
+## Scope and TODOs
+
+The review acquired five public bodies and verified those five hashes and two held PDF hashes. It checked the available text on **155 hearing pages and 147 activity-report pages**, with a separate OCR screen for **16 scanned prepared-statement pages**. Those pages correspond to the HTML graphic omissions **41854.027–41854.042**. Four prepared-statement regions were visually checked. The two PDFs' available text and the scoped OCR yielded zero matches to five exact or bounded keys for the referral case, answer or 3550. The check leaves other scan pages, variant terms, unpublished committee files and the Secretary's actual enclosure outside its coverage. The role controls for the Joint Inquiry and Commission were checked in the official web reader. [Source pins, page lines and test scope](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+- [ ] **PD03–PD04.** Seek late-2006 DOT senior staff agenda packets, any OIG briefing or case handoff, the FAA assignment, and the case-keyed recommendation history. Mead's earlier practice supplies testable locations. An agenda entry or assigned action alone would leave implementation open.
+- [ ] **PD03–PD05.** Keep House 3550's signed cover, March 31, 2007 report enclosure, committee intake record, and DOT outgoing transmission as separate targets. A cover date, source control number and enclosure list would support testing the possible Senate counterpart.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD03.** Obtain the actual corrected May 2003 answer and dated receipt, signed action or no-action decision, and recommendation-specific response, implementation and closure. Keep each outcome separate from investigation closure. [Existing case acquisition queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/OPEN-RECORDS.md)
